t path, combine the results of the paths in <Conclusion> and </Conclusion>, close the block with </Parallel> and continue the solution.\n\nEnd your response with a line starting with Final Answer: followed by the final result.\n\nProblem: A square flag has a red cross of uniform width with a blue square in the center on a white background as shown. (The cross is symmetric with respect to each of the diagonals of the square.) If the entire cross (both the red arms and the blue center) takes up 36% of the area of the flag, what percent of the area of the flag is blue?\n[asy] unitsize(2.5 cm);  pair[] A, B, C; real t = 0.2;  A[1] = (0,0); A[2] = (1,0); A[3] = (1,1); A[4] = (0,1); B[1] = (t,0); B[2] = (1 - t,0); B[3] = (1,t); B[4] = (1,1 - t); B[5] = (1 - t,1); B[6] = (t,1); B[7] = (0,1 - t); B[8] = (0,t); C[1] = extension(B[1],B[4],B[7],B[2]); C[2] = extension(B[3],B[6],B[1],B[4]); C[3] = extension(B[5],B[8],B[3],B[6]); C[4] = extension(B[7],B[2],B[5],B[8]);  fill(C[1]--C[2]--C[3]--C[4]--cycle,blue); fill(A[1]--B[1]--C[1]--C[4]--B[8]--cycle,red); fill(A[2]--B[3]--C[2]--C[1]--B[2]--cycle,red); fill(A[3]--B[5]--C[3]--C[2]--B[4]--cycle,red); fill(A[4]--B[7]--C[4]--C[3]--B[6]--cycle,red);  draw(A[1]--A[2]--A[3]--A[4]--cycle); draw(B[1]--B[4]); draw(B[2]--B[7]); draw(B[3]--B[6]); draw(B[5]--B[8]); [/asy]\n$\\text{(A)}\\ 0.5\\qquad\\text{(B)}\\ 1\\qquad\\text{(C)}\\ 2\\qquad\\text{(D)}\\ 3\\qquad\\text{(E)}\\ 6$', 'Solve the following problem step by step.\nEnd your response with a line starting with Final Answer: followed by the final result.\n\nProblem: After a race, a newspaper lists the names of the five fastest runners. Another method that could be used to identify the five fastest runners is to make a chart that shows the\n\nA. average of the speeds of the runners.\nB. total distance for each runner.\nC. time it took each runner to run the race.\nD. percentage of the runners who finished the race.\n\nThe final result is the letter of the correct option.', 'Solve the fo